{"_id":"68a7362f8ec3d8323af1c594","nodeId":"UIx0XYaOgXXlYbbQtjiPq","roadmapSlug":"python","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:26.571Z","description":"# Threading\n\n[Multithreading](https://roadmap.sh/python/multithreading) allows multiple threads within a single process. However, because of GIL, threads cannot run in parallel on different cores, which makes multithreading suitable for I/O tasks (e.g., network requests) but not for computational tasks.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Python Threading Library","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/threading.html","_id":"6a75d319b0650226a50ae3ec"},{"type":"article","title":"Python Multithreading: The Most Practical Intro","url":"https://roadmap.sh/python/multithreading","_id":"6a75d319b0650226a50ae3ed"},{"type":"article","title":"Introduction to Threading in Python","url":"https://realpython.com/intro-to-python-threading/","_id":"6a75d319b0650226a50ae3ee"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:09.455Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e33faacf8c05faf5e1fd0","title":"DataCamp - Python Programming Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/L0YnzL"},{"_id":"6a5e33fdacf8c05faf5e2124","title":"DataCamp - Python Developer","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/vDW623"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python/content/UIx0XYaOgXXlYbbQtjiPq.md"}